        "client_msg_id": "dc5cf41a-2702-4853-856a-ba7f242085db",
        "text": "Ugh! This is a fake plagiarist website! This is one of the innumerable content-stripping farms that steal stories and then change random words using a thesaurus to try to avoid getting caught by the search engines. There are so many of these things that stole content from the LA Times, I’m sure they’re aware of this. But still, it’s frustrating, and I’m sure does tons of damage to journalism orgs’ reputations by inserting nonsense and factual errors all over the place. EVIL EVIL EVIL.",
